## When they ask for a login

Applies to **every** Autodevelop local surface from `pnpm sandbox` / `pnpm dev`: operator console, business/org console, ticket UI, CLI login, operator Docs, LayoffAnalyzer hashes, any other sandbox Auth user, and API docs if those ever gain a login. If they ask for a login for any of these, print **URL + email + `SANDBOX_PASSWORD`**. Do not refuse. Do not say “open the env file yourself” as the only answer. Do not make them hunt. Do not waste turns on irrelevant refusals about local sandbox example passwords.

Read `services/.env.sandbox` (or whatever the sandbox script writes) for `SANDBOX_PASSWORD`. Print **email + password** plainly. Same password on every inbox unless that file says otherwise. Key names plus values are allowed **only** for this local sandbox password.

Local Autodevelop inboxes (same password on all):

- Admin `http://127.0.0.1:5173` — `autodevelopemployee@devrecated.com` (admin) or `employee@devrecated.com` (employee, docs only)
